claimed: integration-test-gate — separate live/docker-dependent tests (LIVE model, kafka, mongo, pg, tls, redis, s3, spark...) from the default sbt test gate into their own integration-test command, so their occasional flakiness (confirmed multiple times this session: TestChatDemo LIVE, live-model variance) stops polluting the main gate's signal. munit's per-suite tag mechanism (a shared trait tagging every test 'Live' via munitTests() override) + sbt testOptions exclude-tags for default Test, a new command for the tagged run.
